Hi,

By default the covariances of exogenous observed variables are fixed to sample values. From the documentation

fixed.x: If TRUE, the exogenous ‘x’ covariates are considered fixed variables and the means, variances and covariances of these variables are fixed to their sample values. If FALSE, they are considered random, and the means, variances and co- variances are free parameters. If "default", the value is set depending on the mimic option.

You should remove x1~~x2 from the model.

The other warnings are caused by the site invariant variables: these do not have within-site variance, so you cannot estimate their within-site effects.

Mikko

