On 10/10/2015 10:08 AM, FO wrote:
> Sorry for the multiple posts...how is RMSEA calculated?
>
> When I try RMSEA = sqrt((chi-square/(n*d)) - (1/n))*sqrt(g)
>   where n = sample size, g= no. of groups, d=degrees of freedom
>
> I get a different RMSEA then the one that it calculates. Am I doing
> something wrong?

This is the formula used by lavaan (see the file lav_fit_measures.R line
590):

RMSEA <- sqrt( max( c((X2/N)/df - 1/(N), 0) ) ) * sqrt(G)

This looks identical to your formula. So, either one of the ingredients
must be wrong.

Yves.

